IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ira-dates`
IMPORT `ira-rules`

-- Industrial Relations Act 1979 (WA) -- the employee's questions: the seat of the individual employee (worker, or
-- person sexually harassed in connection with work) of an employer in the WA state system who brings or answers a
-- claim. Each question takes plain facts; judgments the Act leaves to the Commission or the industrial magistrate's
-- court are asked as facts ("the Commission considers ..."), never guessed.
--
-- Sourced from the Western Australian Legislation website at 2026-09-07: "Industrial Relations Act 1979", State of
-- Western Australia, licensed under CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). See SOURCE-LICENSE.md.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Industrial Relations Act 1979 -- the employee`

§§ `Am I covered (s 7, s 7A, s 24A, s 80A)`

@export Is my employment in the Western Australian state industrial relations system (the Industrial Relations Act 1979), rather than the national system under the Fair Work Act 2009? Yes if my employer is not a national system employer (for example a sole trader, a partnership, an unincorporated association or a non-trading body) or is declared under s 80A; otherwise the Fair Work Act decides and this Act gives no answer.
GIVEN `my employer is a national system employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employer a national system employer under the Fair Work Act 2009 s 14 (for example a trading or financial corporation such as a Pty Ltd company, or the Commonwealth)?
      `my employer is declared under section 80A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employer one of the WA local governments or regional local governments listed in the Industrial Relations (General) Regulations 1997 Schedule 4, declared under s 80A not to be national system employers (from 1 January 2023)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my employment in the WA state system` `my employer is a national system employer` `my employer is declared under section 80A` MEANS
    `the state system reaches the employment` `my employer is a national system employer` `my employer is declared under section 80A`
    -- NOTHING-kind: points outside the text (a national system employer not declared: the FW Act decides)

@export Am I an employee under the Industrial Relations Act 1979 s 7 (with s 7A: judged by the real substance, practical reality and true nature of the relationship, not just the contract's label)?
GIVEN `in substance I am employed by the person I work for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Looking at the whole relationship, including how the contract is performed in practice, are you in substance employed by the person you work for (s 7A)?
      `I work for hire or reward` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you work for pay or other reward (an apprentice counts)?
      `my usual status is that of an employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your usual status that of an employee?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Am I an employee under the Act` `in substance I am employed by the person I work for` `I work for hire or reward` `my usual status is that of an employee` MEANS
    `an employee under section 7` `in substance I am employed by the person I work for` `I work for hire or reward` `my usual status is that of an employee`

@export If the other side says I was not their employee, must they prove it (s 24A in the Commission, s 81CAA in the industrial magistrate's court)?
GIVEN `I carry or carried out work for the other party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you carry out, or did you carry out, work for the other party?
      `the other party claims I am not its employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the other party claim you are, or were, not its employee?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must the other party prove I was not their employee` `I carry or carried out work for the other party` `the other party claims I am not its employee` MEANS
    IF `I carry or carried out work for the other party` AND `the other party claims I am not its employee`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind: silent (the sections speak only of their own case)

§§ `Unfair dismissal (only if you have been dismissed)`

@export Can the Industrial Relations Commission determine my claim that I was harshly, oppressively or unfairly dismissed (s 29(1)(c), s 29AA(1)-(3))? Checks the state system, an application to the Fair Work Commission, and the high-income bar. The time limit is a separate question.
GIVEN `my employer is a national system employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employer a national system employer under the Fair Work Act 2009 s 14 (for example a Pty Ltd company)?
      `my employer is declared under section 80A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employer one of the WA local governments or regional local governments listed in the Industrial Relations (General) Regulations 1997 Schedule 4, declared under s 80A not to be national system employers (from 1 January 2023)?
      `I was the employee of the employer who dismissed me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you that employer's employee (s 7)?
      `I applied to the Fair Work Commission about this dismissal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you lodged an application with the Fair Work Commission for relief about the end of this employment?
      `that application was withdrawn or rejected for want of jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that Fair Work Commission application withdrawn, or rejected or dismissed because the Fair Work Commission had no jurisdiction? (No if you made none.)
      `an industrial instrument applies to my employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an award, an industrial agreement, an employer-employee agreement or a Commission order apply to your employment?
      `my contract salary` IS A NUMBER @desc Your salary under your contract of employment, in dollars a year, worked out as the Regulations r 5(2) say.
      `the prescribed amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The prescribed amount in force: $90 000 a year as indexed each 1 July under the Regulations r 6 (the Commission publishes the figure).
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the Commission determine my unfair dismissal claim` `my employer is a national system employer` `my employer is declared under section 80A` `I was the employee of the employer who dismissed me` `I applied to the Fair Work Commission about this dismissal` `that application was withdrawn or rejected for want of jurisdiction` `an industrial instrument applies to my employment` `my contract salary` `the prescribed amount` MEANS
    IF `the state system reaches the employment` `my employer is a national system employer` `my employer is declared under section 80A` EQUALS NOTHING
    THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind: points outside the text (the FW Act decides)
    ELSE IF NOT `I was the employee of the employer who dismissed me`
         THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind: limited by its own wording (s 29(1)(c) is "a claim by an employee")
         ELSE IF `I applied to the Fair Work Commission about this dismissal` AND (NOT `that application was withdrawn or rejected for want of jurisdiction`)
              THEN JUST FALSE    -- s 29AA(1): "must not determine"
              ELSE IF `the salary bar applies` `an industrial instrument applies to my employment` `my contract salary` `the prescribed amount`
                   THEN JUST FALSE    -- s 29AA(3)
                   ELSE JUST TRUE

@export By when must I refer my unfair dismissal claim to the Industrial Relations Commission (s 29(2)(a): no later than 28 days after the day my employment ended; a last day on a Saturday or Sunday moves to the Monday)?
GIVEN `the day my employment was terminated` IS A DATE @desc The day your employment was terminated.
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I refer my unfair dismissal claim` `the day my employment was terminated` MEANS
    `the time limit of` 28 `days after` `the day my employment was terminated`

@export Is my unfair dismissal referral in time on this day, or, if late, will it be accepted (s 29(2)(a), (3): the Commission may accept a late referral if it considers it would be unfair not to)?
GIVEN `the day my employment was terminated` IS A DATE @desc The day your employment was terminated.
      `the day I refer the claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you lodge (or plan to lodge) the referral with the Commission.
      `the Commission considers it unfair not to accept a late referral` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the referral is late: does the Commission consider it would be unfair not to accept it? (Ignored if in time.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my unfair dismissal referral in time or accepted` `the day my employment was terminated` `the day I refer the claim` `the Commission considers it unfair not to accept a late referral` MEANS
    IF `the day I refer the claim` `is before` `the day my employment was terminated`
    THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind: silent (a referral before the employment ends)
    ELSE IF `the employee` `takes` `refer the unfair dismissal claim` `from` `the day my employment was terminated` `by` (`By when must I refer my unfair dismissal claim` `the day my employment was terminated`) `on` `the day I refer the claim` `in time`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE IF `the Commission considers it unfair not to accept a late referral`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE

@export Is my dismissal one the Commission must weigh specially in deciding whether it was unfair: within a short probation (agreed probation and under 3 months on it), or work in a private home for the employer or their family or household (s 23A(2))?
GIVEN `I was on an agreed probationary period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the dismissal, were you employed for a probationary period agreed with your employer?
      `months I had been employed on probation` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months had you been employed on that probationary basis at the dismissal? (0 if none.)
      `I was employed in a private home serving the employer or their household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you employed in a private home to provide services directly to the employer or a member of their family or household?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is my dismissal one the Commission must weigh specially` `I was on an agreed probationary period` `months I had been employed on probation` `I was employed in a private home serving the employer or their household` MEANS
        (`I was on an agreed probationary period` AND `months I had been employed on probation` LESS THAN 3)
    OR  `I was employed in a private home serving the employer or their household`

@export Which orders can the Commission make for my unfair dismissal (s 23A(1), (3)-(6)): reinstatement, or re-employment if reinstatement is impracticable, each with continuity and lost pay; compensation only if both are impracticable?
GIVEN `the Commission determines my dismissal was unfair` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission determined that your dismissal was harsh, oppressive or unfair?
      `the Commission considers reinstatement impracticable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Commission consider reinstating you to your former position would be impracticable?
      `the Commission considers re-employment impracticable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Commission consider re-employing you in another suitable position the employer has available would be impracticable?
GIVETH A LIST OF `Remedy`
`Which orders can the Commission make for my unfair dismissal` `the Commission determines my dismissal was unfair` `the Commission considers reinstatement impracticable` `the Commission considers re-employment impracticable` MEANS
    IF NOT `the Commission determines my dismissal was unfair`
    THEN EMPTY
    ELSE IF NOT `the Commission considers reinstatement impracticable`
         THEN LIST `reinstatement to my former position`, `an order maintaining the continuity of my employment`, `payment of the remuneration I lost because of the dismissal`
         ELSE IF NOT `the Commission considers re-employment impracticable`
              THEN LIST `re-employment in another suitable position`, `an order maintaining the continuity of my employment`, `payment of the remuneration I lost because of the dismissal`
              ELSE LIST `compensation for loss or injury caused by the dismissal`

@export Can the Commission order my employer to pay me compensation for my unfair dismissal (s 23A(6): if, and only if, reinstatement or re-employment would be impracticable)?
GIVEN `the Commission determines my dismissal was unfair` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission determined that your dismissal was harsh, oppressive or unfair?
      `the Commission considers reinstatement impracticable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Commission consider reinstating you would be impracticable?
      `the Commission considers re-employment impracticable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Commission consider re-employing you in another suitable available position would be impracticable?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I be awarded compensation for my unfair dismissal` `the Commission determines my dismissal was unfair` `the Commission considers reinstatement impracticable` `the Commission considers re-employment impracticable` MEANS
    JUST (    `the Commission determines my dismissal was unfair`
          AND `the Commission considers reinstatement impracticable`
          AND `the Commission considers re-employment impracticable`)

@export What is the most compensation the Commission can order for my unfair dismissal (s 23A(8), (9): 6 months' remuneration, which may be worked out from an average rate)?
GIVEN `my remuneration for a year` IS A NUMBER @desc Your remuneration for a year, in dollars (the Commission may use an average rate over a relevant period of employment).
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most compensation for my unfair dismissal` `my remuneration for a year` MEANS
    `my remuneration for a year` DIVIDED BY 2

@export What salary counts for the high-income bar on unfair dismissal and contractual benefit claims, if I was continuously employed by the employer for the 12 months before the dismissal or claim without leave without full pay (Regulations r 5(2)(a): the greater of what I received and what I was entitled to)?
GIVEN `I was continuously employed for the 12 months before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you continuously employed by this employer for the whole 12 months immediately before the dismissal or claim?
      `I took leave without full pay in those 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you on leave without full pay at any time in those 12 months?
      `the salary I received in those 12 months` IS A NUMBER @desc The salary you actually received in those 12 months, in dollars.
      `the salary I was entitled to in those 12 months` IS A NUMBER @desc The salary you were entitled to receive in those 12 months, in dollars.
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What salary counts for the high-income bar` `I was continuously employed for the 12 months before` `I took leave without full pay in those 12 months` `the salary I received in those 12 months` `the salary I was entitled to in those 12 months` MEANS
    IF `I was continuously employed for the 12 months before` AND (NOT `I took leave without full pay in those 12 months`)
    THEN JUST (IF `the salary I received in those 12 months` GREATER THAN `the salary I was entitled to in those 12 months`
               THEN `the salary I received in those 12 months`
               ELSE `the salary I was entitled to in those 12 months`)
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind: points outside the text (r 5(2)(b), (c) formulas lost in the deposited text)

§§ `Denied contractual benefits (only if your employer has not given you a benefit your contract promises)`

@export Can the Industrial Relations Commission determine my claim that my employer has not allowed me a benefit I am entitled to under my contract of employment (s 29(1)(d), s 29AA(4))? Not for a benefit under an award or order (that is enforced in the industrial magistrate's court), and not if the high-income bar applies. The Act sets no time limit for this claim.
GIVEN `my employer is a national system employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employer a national system employer under the Fair Work Act 2009 s 14 (for example a Pty Ltd company)?
      `my employer is declared under section 80A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employer one of the WA local governments or regional local governments listed in the Industrial Relations (General) Regulations 1997 Schedule 4, declared under s 80A not to be national system employers (from 1 January 2023)?
      `I am entitled to the benefit under my contract of employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to the benefit under your contract of employment?
      `the benefit is under an award or Commission order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the benefit one under an award or an order of the Commission?
      `an industrial instrument applies to my employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an award, an industrial agreement, an employer-employee agreement or a Commission order apply to your employment?
      `my contract salary` IS A NUMBER @desc Your salary under your contract of employment, in dollars a year, worked out as the Regulations r 5(2) say.
      `the prescribed amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The prescribed amount in force: $90 000 a year as indexed each 1 July under the Regulations r 6.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the Commission determine my contractual benefit claim` `my employer is a national system employer` `my employer is declared under section 80A` `I am entitled to the benefit under my contract of employment` `the benefit is under an award or Commission order` `an industrial instrument applies to my employment` `my contract salary` `the prescribed amount` MEANS
    IF `the state system reaches the employment` `my employer is a national system employer` `my employer is declared under section 80A` EQUALS NOTHING
    THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind: points outside the text (the FW Act decides)
    ELSE IF `the benefit is under an award or Commission order`
         THEN JUST FALSE    -- "(other than X)": fork F6
         ELSE IF NOT `I am entitled to the benefit under my contract of employment`
              THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind: limited by its own wording
              ELSE IF `the salary bar applies` `an industrial instrument applies to my employment` `my contract salary` `the prescribed amount`
                   THEN JUST FALSE    -- s 29AA(4)
                   ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `Unpaid entitlements and enforcement in the industrial magistrate's court (only if your employer has not complied)`

@export Can I apply myself to the industrial magistrate's court to enforce an entitlement (s 83(1)(e), (3)): an award, industrial agreement or order that applies to me, or my entitlement under the Long Service Leave Act Part III, the Minimum Conditions of Employment Act or a local government long service leave provision?
GIVEN `the award, agreement or order applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the entitlement in an award, industrial agreement, employer-employee agreement or Commission order that you are a party to or that applies to you?
      `the entitlement is under the LSL Act, the MCE Act or a local government provision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it instead an entitlement that applies to you under the Long Service Leave Act 1958 Part III, the Minimum Conditions of Employment Act 1993, or a local government long service leave provision?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I apply to enforce my entitlement` `the award, agreement or order applies to me` `the entitlement is under the LSL Act, the MCE Act or a local government provision` MEANS
    JUST (`the award, agreement or order applies to me` OR `the entitlement is under the LSL Act, the MCE Act or a local government provision`)
    -- s 83(3): no other route, so JUST FALSE where neither holds

@export By when must I apply to the industrial magistrate's court to enforce an entitlement, a s 23A unfair dismissal order or a civil penalty provision (s 82A: within 6 years after the day of the contravention or failure; a last day on a Saturday or Sunday moves to the Monday)?
GIVEN `the day of the contravention` IS A DATE @desc The day the contravention or failure to comply is alleged to have taken place.
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I apply to the industrial magistrate's court` `the day of the contravention` MEANS
    `the time limit of` 6 `years after` `the day of the contravention`

@export Is my application to the industrial magistrate's court in time on this day (s 82A: within 6 years after the day of the contravention)?
GIVEN `the day of the contravention` IS A DATE @desc The day the contravention or failure to comply is alleged to have taken place.
      `the day I apply` IS A DATE @desc The day you make (or plan to make) the application.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my application to the industrial magistrate's court in time` `the day of the contravention` `the day I apply` MEANS
    IF `the day I apply` `is before` `the day of the contravention`
    THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind: silent (an application before the contravention)
    ELSE JUST (`the employee` `takes` `apply to the industrial magistrate's court` `from` `the day of the contravention` `by` (`By when must I apply to the industrial magistrate's court` `the day of the contravention`) `on` `the day I apply` `in time`)

@export From what day back can an order to pay me what I was underpaid reach (s 83A(2): amounts for a period no more than 6 years before the proceedings began, or, if my employer failed to produce records or answer truthfully, no more than 6 years before that failure)?
GIVEN `the day the proceedings began` IS A DATE @desc The day your proceedings under s 83 began.
      `my employer failed to produce records or answer truthfully` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your employer been found to have failed to produce or allow examination of a relevant record, or to answer a relevant question truthfully (s 102(1)(a) or (b))?
      `the day of that failure` IS A DATE @desc The day of that failure (any date if there was none).
GIVETH A DATE
`From what day can my underpayment be ordered` `the day the proceedings began` `my employer failed to produce records or answer truthfully` `the day of that failure` MEANS
    IF `my employer failed to produce records or answer truthfully`
    THEN `the earlier of` (`the earliest day of` 6 `years before` `the day the proceedings began`) `and` (`the earliest day of` 6 `years before` `the day of that failure`)
    ELSE `the earliest day of` 6 `years before` `the day the proceedings began`

@export If my employer did not keep the records or give the pay slips the law required, must my employer disprove what I allege about that matter (s 83EB)?
GIVEN `my employer had to keep a record or give a pay slip about the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your employer required by the Act, the Long Service Leave Act or a local government long service leave provision to make or keep a record, give a pay slip, or make a record available, about the matter?
      `my employer failed to do so` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer fail to comply with that requirement?
      `the court accepts my employer's excuse as reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court accept that your employer has a reasonable excuse for the failure?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must my employer disprove my allegation` `my employer had to keep a record or give a pay slip about the matter` `my employer failed to do so` `the court accepts my employer's excuse as reasonable` MEANS
    JUST (    `my employer had to keep a record or give a pay slip about the matter`
          AND `my employer failed to do so`
          AND (NOT `the court accepts my employer's excuse as reasonable`))

@export Was my employer's contravention a serious contravention (s 83EA(2)-(4): done knowingly, or recklessly, aware of a substantial risk it would occur when that risk was unjustifiable to take)?
GIVEN `my employer knowingly contravened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer knowingly commit the contravention (for a company: expressly, tacitly or impliedly authorise it)?
      `my employer was aware of a substantial risk of the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your employer aware of a substantial risk that the contravention would occur?
      `it was unjustifiable to take that risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Given the circumstances known to your employer, was it unjustifiable to take that risk?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Was it a serious contravention` `my employer knowingly contravened` `my employer was aware of a substantial risk of the contravention` `it was unjustifiable to take that risk` MEANS
    `a serious contravention` `my employer knowingly contravened` `my employer was aware of a substantial risk of the contravention` `it was unjustifiable to take that risk`

@export What is the most the industrial magistrate's court can order my employer to pay as a pecuniary penalty for contravening an entitlement provision or a civil penalty provision (s 83(4A), s 83E(1))?
GIVEN `my employer is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employer a body corporate (a company or other incorporated body), rather than an individual?
      `my employer knowingly contravened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer knowingly commit the contravention?
      `my employer was aware of a substantial risk of the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your employer aware of a substantial risk that the contravention would occur?
      `it was unjustifiable to take that risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Given the circumstances known to your employer, was it unjustifiable to take that risk?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most my employer can be penalised` `my employer is a body corporate` `my employer knowingly contravened` `my employer was aware of a substantial risk of the contravention` `it was unjustifiable to take that risk` MEANS
    `the maximum pecuniary penalty for` `the kind` (`a serious contravention` `my employer knowingly contravened` `my employer was aware of a substantial risk of the contravention` `it was unjustifiable to take that risk`)
    WHERE
        `the kind` MEANS IF `my employer is a body corporate` THEN `a body corporate` ELSE `an individual`

@export Can I apply myself to the industrial magistrate's court for a civil penalty order (s 83E(6)(a): a person directly affected by the contravention may; a compliance notice under s 84T(1) is for an industrial inspector only)?
GIVEN `I am directly affected by the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you directly affected by the contravention?
      `the provision is a compliance notice under section 84T` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contravention a failure to comply with a compliance notice (s 84T(1))?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I apply for a civil penalty order` `I am directly affected by the contravention` `the provision is a compliance notice under section 84T` MEANS
    IF `the provision is a compliance notice under section 84T`
    THEN JUST FALSE    -- s 84T: "may only be made by an industrial inspector"
    ELSE IF `I am directly affected by the contravention`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind: limited by its own wording (an organisation of which you are a member may, s 83E(6)(b))

§§ `Enforcing an unfair dismissal order (only if your employer has not reinstated or re-employed you as ordered)`

@export If my employer does not comply with an order to reinstate or re-employ me and the court revokes it, what is the least the court can order my employer to pay me instead (s 83B(3)(a)(ii), (7)(a): 6 months' remuneration)?
GIVEN `my remuneration for a year` IS A NUMBER @desc Your remuneration for a year, in dollars (the court may use an average rate over a relevant period of employment).
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the least the court can order if my reinstatement order is not complied with` `my remuneration for a year` MEANS
    `my remuneration for a year` DIVIDED BY 2

@export If my employer does not comply with an order to reinstate or re-employ me and the court revokes it, what is the most the court can order my employer to pay me instead (s 83B(7)(b): 12 months' remuneration, on top of which lost remuneration may be ordered under s 83B(5)(b))?
GIVEN `my remuneration for a year` IS A NUMBER @desc Your remuneration for a year, in dollars (the court may use an average rate over a relevant period of employment).
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most the court can order if my reinstatement order is not complied with` `my remuneration for a year` MEANS
    `my remuneration for a year`

§§ `Bullying at work (only if you think you are being bullied)`

@export Am I a worker for the bullying and sexual harassment provisions (s 51BH, with s 51BG): anyone who carries out work in any capacity for a person conducting a business or undertaking (employee, contractor, labour hire worker, outworker, apprentice, student on work experience, volunteer), and a police officer?
GIVEN `I carry out work for a person conducting a business or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you carry out work in any capacity for a person (or partnership, unincorporated association or public authority) conducting a business or undertaking, whether or not for profit?
      `the business is a volunteer association employing no one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that business or undertaking a volunteer association: volunteers working together for community purposes, none of whom employs anyone to carry out work for it?
      `I am a police officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a police officer of WA Police?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Am I a worker` `I carry out work for a person conducting a business or undertaking` `the business is a volunteer association employing no one` `I am a police officer` MEANS
        (`I carry out work for a person conducting a business or undertaking` AND (NOT `the business is a volunteer association employing no one`))
    OR  `I am a police officer`

@export Was I bullied at work (s 51BI): while I was at work, did someone repeatedly behave unreasonably towards me (or a group of workers I belong to) in a way that created a risk to my health or safety, other than reasonable management action carried out in a reasonable manner?
GIVEN `it happened while I was at work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the behaviour happen while you were at work?
      `a person repeatedly behaved unreasonably towards me or my group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a person, alone or in a group, repeatedly behave unreasonably towards you or a group of workers you belong to?
      `the behaviour created a risk to my health or safety` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did that behaviour create a risk to your health or safety?
      `it was reasonable management action done reasonably` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it reasonable management action carried out in a reasonable manner?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Was I bullied at work` `it happened while I was at work` `a person repeatedly behaved unreasonably towards me or my group` `the behaviour created a risk to my health or safety` `it was reasonable management action done reasonably` MEANS
        `it happened while I was at work`
    AND `a person repeatedly behaved unreasonably towards me or my group`
    AND `the behaviour created a risk to my health or safety`
    AND (NOT `it was reasonable management action done reasonably`)

@export Can I apply to the Industrial Relations Commission for a stop bullying order (s 51BJ(1))? A stop bullying order cannot award compensation (s 51BM(3)).
GIVEN `I carry out work for a person conducting a business or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you carry out work in any capacity for a person conducting a business or undertaking?
      `the business is a volunteer association employing no one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that business or undertaking a volunteer association whose volunteers employ no one?
      `I am a police officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a police officer of WA Police?
      `I reasonably believe I have been bullied at work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you reasonably believe you have been bullied at work?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I apply for a stop bullying order` `I carry out work for a person conducting a business or undertaking` `the business is a volunteer association employing no one` `I am a police officer` `I reasonably believe I have been bullied at work` MEANS
    IF `Am I a worker` `I carry out work for a person conducting a business or undertaking` `the business is a volunteer association employing no one` `I am a police officer` AND `I reasonably believe I have been bullied at work`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind: limited by its own wording (s 51BJ grants the application to a worker who so believes)

@export By when must the Commission start to deal with my stop bullying or stop sexual harassment application (ss 51BK(1), 51BV(1): within 14 days after it is made; a last day on a Saturday or Sunday moves to the Monday)?
GIVEN `the day I made the application` IS A DATE @desc The day you made the stop bullying or stop sexual harassment application.
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must the Commission start to deal with my application` `the day I made the application` MEANS
    `the time limit of` 14 `days after` `the day I made the application`

§§ `Sexual harassment in connection with work (only if you have been sexually harassed)`

@export Was I sexually harassed in connection with work (s 51BQ, s 51BR): an unwelcome sexual advance, request for sexual favours or other conduct of a sexual nature, where a reasonable person would have anticipated I might be offended, humiliated or intimidated, in connection with my being a worker or seeking to become one?
GIVEN `there was an unwelcome sexual advance, request or conduct towards me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did someone make an unwelcome sexual advance or request for sexual favours to you, or engage in other unwelcome conduct of a sexual nature in relation to you (including sexual statements about you, online or otherwise)?
      `a reasonable person would have anticipated I might be offended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Having regard to all the circumstances, would a reasonable person have anticipated the possibility that you would be offended, humiliated or intimidated?
      `it was in connection with my being or seeking to become a worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it in connection with your being a worker, or your seeking to become a worker in a particular business or undertaking?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Was I sexually harassed in connection with work` `there was an unwelcome sexual advance, request or conduct towards me` `a reasonable person would have anticipated I might be offended` `it was in connection with my being or seeking to become a worker` MEANS
        `there was an unwelcome sexual advance, request or conduct towards me`
    AND `a reasonable person would have anticipated I might be offended`
    AND `it was in connection with my being or seeking to become a worker`

@export Is the harasser's employer (or principal, for an agent) treated as having sexually harassed me too (s 51BS), unless it proves it took all reasonable steps to prevent it?
GIVEN `I was sexually harassed in connection with work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you sexually harassed in connection with work?
      `the harasser was an employee or agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the harasser an employee of a person, or an agent engaged by a person?
      `it was in connection with their employment or duties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the harasser do it in connection with their employment, or with their duties as agent?
      `the principal proves it took all reasonable steps to prevent it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the employer or principal prove it took all reasonable steps to prevent the employee or agent sexually harassing people in connection with work?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is the harasser's employer liable too` `I was sexually harassed in connection with work` `the harasser was an employee or agent` `it was in connection with their employment or duties` `the principal proves it took all reasonable steps to prevent it` MEANS
    JUST (    `I was sexually harassed in connection with work`
          AND `the harasser was an employee or agent`
          AND `it was in connection with their employment or duties`
          AND (NOT `the principal proves it took all reasonable steps to prevent it`))

@export Can I refer my sexual harassment allegation to the Industrial Relations Commission (s 51BT(1)(b), s 51BZD(2), (4))? Not while the same allegation is before the industrial magistrate's court as a civil penalty application, or under anti-discrimination legislation, unless that was withdrawn or failed for want of jurisdiction.
GIVEN `I applied to the industrial magistrate's court for a civil penalty on this allegation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you (or someone) applied under s 83E to enforce s 51BR(1) as a civil penalty provision on the same allegation?
      `that application was withdrawn or failed for want of jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that s 83E application withdrawn, or did it fail for want of jurisdiction? (No if none.)
      `I complained under anti-discrimination legislation on this allegation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made a complaint or application on the same allegation under anti-discrimination legislation (the Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (WA), the Sex Discrimination Act 1984, the Australian Human Rights Commission Act 1986, the Fair Work Act 2009, or another State's or Territory's anti-discrimination Act listed in s 51BZD(1))?
      `that complaint was withdrawn or failed for want of jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that complaint or application withdrawn, or did it fail for want of jurisdiction? (No if none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I refer my sexual harassment allegation to the Commission` `I applied to the industrial magistrate's court for a civil penalty on this allegation` `that application was withdrawn or failed for want of jurisdiction` `I complained under anti-discrimination legislation on this allegation` `that complaint was withdrawn or failed for want of jurisdiction` MEANS
    JUST (    (NOT (`I applied to the industrial magistrate's court for a civil penalty on this allegation` AND (NOT `that application was withdrawn or failed for want of jurisdiction`)))
          AND (NOT (`I complained under anti-discrimination legislation on this allegation` AND (NOT `that complaint was withdrawn or failed for want of jurisdiction`))))

@export Can I apply to the industrial magistrate's court for a civil penalty against the person who sexually harassed me in connection with work (s 51BR(3), s 83E(6)(a), s 51BZD(3), (4))? Not while the same allegation is referred to the Commission or under anti-discrimination legislation, unless that was withdrawn or failed for want of jurisdiction.
GIVEN `I referred this allegation to the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a referral been made to the Commission under s 29 on the same allegation?
      `that referral was withdrawn or failed for want of jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that referral withdrawn, or did it fail for want of jurisdiction? (No if none.)
      `I complained under anti-discrimination legislation on this allegation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made a complaint or application on the same allegation under anti-discrimination legislation listed in s 51BZD(1)?
      `that complaint was withdrawn or failed for want of jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that complaint or application withdrawn, or did it fail for want of jurisdiction? (No if none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I apply for a civil penalty for the sexual harassment` `I referred this allegation to the Commission` `that referral was withdrawn or failed for want of jurisdiction` `I complained under anti-discrimination legislation on this allegation` `that complaint was withdrawn or failed for want of jurisdiction` MEANS
    JUST (    (NOT (`I referred this allegation to the Commission` AND (NOT `that referral was withdrawn or failed for want of jurisdiction`)))
          AND (NOT (`I complained under anti-discrimination legislation on this allegation` AND (NOT `that complaint was withdrawn or failed for want of jurisdiction`))))

@export What is the last day on which I can start a sexual harassment proceeding in the Commission without it being open to dismissal for delay (s 51BU: the Commission may dismiss a proceeding started more than 24 months after the last alleged instance)?
GIVEN `the day of the last instance of harassment` IS A DATE @desc The day of the alleged instance, or the last alleged instance, of sexual harassment in connection with work.
GIVETH A DATE
`What is the last day to start my sexual harassment proceeding` `the day of the last instance of harassment` MEANS
    `the last day of` 2 `years after` `the day of the last instance of harassment`

@export Can the Commission dismiss my sexual harassment proceeding because it was started more than 24 months after the last alleged instance (s 51BU)? Within 24 months, s 51BU gives no answer either way.
GIVEN `the day of the last instance of harassment` IS A DATE @desc The day of the alleged instance, or the last alleged instance, of sexual harassment in connection with work.
      `the day I start the proceeding` IS A DATE @desc The day you make the stop sexual harassment application or the referral.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my sexual harassment proceeding be dismissed as late` `the day of the last instance of harassment` `the day I start the proceeding` MEANS
    IF `the day I start the proceeding` `is after` (`What is the last day to start my sexual harassment proceeding` `the day of the last instance of harassment`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind: limited by its own wording (s 51BU's power arises only after 24 months)

§§ `Damaging action and sham contracting (only if your employer acted against you)`

@export Did my employer contravene s 97A by taking damaging action against me (dismissing me, disadvantaging me, refusing to promote or transfer me, otherwise injuring me, refusing to employ me, or threatening any of these) because I can make, made or proposed to make an employment-related inquiry or complaint? Once the action is proved, my employer must prove it was not because of the inquiry or complaint (s 97A(2)).
GIVEN `what my employer did` IS AN `Action taken against me` @desc What your employer (or former or prospective employer) did, from the s 97 list, or none of these.
      `I made or proposed to make an employment-related inquiry or complaint` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you able to make, or did you make or propose to make, an employment-related inquiry or complaint to your employer or another person?
      `my employer proves it was not because of the inquiry or complaint` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your employer prove it did not take the action because you made or proposed to make the inquiry or complaint?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Did my employer take unlawful damaging action against me` `what my employer did` `I made or proposed to make an employment-related inquiry or complaint` `my employer proves it was not because of the inquiry or complaint` MEANS
    JUST (    `is damaging action` `what my employer did`
          AND `I made or proposed to make an employment-related inquiry or complaint`
          AND (NOT `my employer proves it was not because of the inquiry or complaint`))

@export Did my employer contravene s 97D by telling me my contract of employment was a contract for services (that I was a contractor), unless my employer proves it did not know and could not reasonably have known it was a contract of employment?
GIVEN `my employer told me my contract was a contract for services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer represent to you that your contract is a contract for services (that you are an independent contractor)?
      `my contract is in truth a contract of employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract in truth a contract of employment (judged by the real substance of the relationship, s 7A)?
      `my employer proves it did not and could not reasonably have known` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your employer prove that, when it made the representation, it did not know and could not reasonably be expected to have known that the contract was one of employment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Did my employer misrepresent my employment as contracting` `my employer told me my contract was a contract for services` `my contract is in truth a contract of employment` `my employer proves it did not and could not reasonably have known` MEANS
    JUST (    `my employer told me my contract was a contract for services`
          AND `my contract is in truth a contract of employment`
          AND (NOT `my employer proves it did not and could not reasonably have known`))

@export Did my employer contravene s 97E by dismissing me, or threatening to, in order to engage me as a contractor to do the same or substantially the same work? Once the dismissal or threat is proved, my employer must prove that was not its purpose (s 97E(2)).
GIVEN `my employer dismissed or threatened to dismiss me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer dismiss you, or threaten to dismiss you, while you were doing particular work for it?
      `my employer proves it was not to engage me as a contractor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your employer prove it did not do so in order to engage you under a contract for services for the same or substantially the same work?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Did my employer dismiss me to engage me as a contractor` `my employer dismissed or threatened to dismiss me` `my employer proves it was not to engage me as a contractor` MEANS
    JUST (`my employer dismissed or threatened to dismiss me` AND (NOT `my employer proves it was not to engage me as a contractor`))

@export Once the industrial magistrate's court finds my employer took damaging action (s 97A) or engaged in sham contracting (ss 97D-97F), can it order my employer to reinstate me, employ me or compensate me (ss 97B, 97G)? Not if I have applied elsewhere for relief for the same action, unless that was withdrawn or failed for want of jurisdiction.
GIVEN `the court found my employer contravened s 97A, 97D, 97E or 97F` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the industrial magistrate's court determined that your employer contravened s 97A(1), 97D(1), 97E(1) or 97F(1) in respect of you?
      `I applied elsewhere for relief for the same action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you applied under another provision of the Act or another law (for example an unfair dismissal claim) for relief for the same action?
      `that other application was withdrawn or failed for want of jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that other application withdrawn, or did it fail for want of jurisdiction? (No if none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the court order reinstatement, employment or compensation for me` `the court found my employer contravened s 97A, 97D, 97E or 97F` `I applied elsewhere for relief for the same action` `that other application was withdrawn or failed for want of jurisdiction` MEANS
    JUST (    `the court found my employer contravened s 97A, 97D, 97E or 97F`
          AND (NOT (`I applied elsewhere for relief for the same action` AND (NOT `that other application was withdrawn or failed for want of jurisdiction`))))
